 283:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
 284:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  This function is used to back up application-specific data into the flash.
 285:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
 286:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  This function works in two Write modes: blocking or non-blocking:
 287:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  * Blocking (#CY_BLE_STORE_DATA_MODE_BLOCKING) - The function writes
 288:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    all data from srcBuff and returns #CY_BLE_SUCCESS when finished.
 289:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  <br>
 290:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  * Non-blocking (#CY_BLE_STORE_DATA_MODE_NON_BLOCKING) - The function initiates
 291:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    Write data and returns #CY_BLE_INFO_FLASH_WRITE_IN_PROGRESS when the Write
 292:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    is in progress, or #CY_BLE_SUCCESS when finished. In order to write complete
 293:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    data, the application needs to continue calling this function with
 294:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    the same input parameter (param), until this function returns CY_BLE_SUCCESS.
 295:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    The application must not change the input parameter's structure and content
 296:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *    until this function returns CY_BLE_SUCCESS.
 297:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
 298:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  \param param: The parameter of type \ref cy_stc_ble_app_flash_param_t.
 299:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *   * param->srcBuff:   The source buffer.
 300:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *   * param->destAddr:  The destination address. The destination buffer size
 301:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *                       should be greater than or equal to the source buffer.
 302:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *   * param->buffLen:   The length of srcData (in bytes).
 303:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *   * param->writeMode: Blocking or non-blocking Write mode.
 304:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
 305:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  param->destAddr - An array address to be defined in the
 306:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  application and aligned to the size of the device's flash row.
 307:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
 308:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  An example of a declaration of such an array (100 bytes):
 309:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *   - CY_ALIGN(CY_FLASH_SIZEOF_ROW) const uint8_t appBuff[100u] = {0u}; <br>
 310:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  <br>
 311:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  CY_ALIGN() - Aligns the array to the size of the device`s flash row.
 312:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  Even if the length of srcData is not a multiple of the flash row size,
 313:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  Cy_BLE_StoreAppData() forms whole rows, and programs them in sequence.
 314:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *
 315:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\middleware\ble/cy_ble_gap.c **** *  The approximate time to write one row - 16ms.
